  "result": "The node did not pass: the final gate verdict is **WITNESS_FAIL**. Five of the seven witnesses pass (forbid, permit, idle, blind, branch_3), but branch_1 and branch_2 can never come out as planned, because of how the run's reading classifies two vehicle groups.\n\n**The rule** (`LVMC_11_52_030_B.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** vehicles, per the `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle` group.\n- **When it applies:** the subject is in a curb zone painted yellow. It does not apply when the subject is a commercial vehicle or a taxicab and a `parking_restricted` zone sign governs a lane the subject is in, with the sign's posted conditions holding for it.\n- **The duty:** the subject must not come to a halt there, using `p.halt_speed_tolerance` as the \"at rest\" threshold.\n\nI made no reading choices of my own, so `narrowings` is empty.\n\n**Why branch_1 and branch_2 fail:** in the run's reading, `DEF-LVMC-11-02-070::commercial_vehicle` and `DEF-LVMC-11-02-140::taxicab` include no vehicle class at all; every class is left unresolved, even taxicab under the taxicab group. Core then treats membership as unknown for every vehicle and never as true. So a commercial van or taxicab halting in the zone while the sign's conditions hold gives \"unknown\" instead of the planned \"not applicable\". The scenes do satisfy the sign's conditions; only the group membership is undecided. The rules don't allow me to fix this by swapping in the plain commercial-vehicle or taxicab class.\n\n**What needs to change upstream:** either the reading classifies those groups (at least taxicab under the taxicab group, and the classes the commercial-vehicle definition covers), or the plan changes branch_1 and branch_2 to expect \"unknown\" or drops them.\n\n**Gate budget:** I used 3 of 6 runs, and 2 of them were my mistakes. On the first I piped the gate command into `head`, which the rules forbid. The second I started by accident on the unchanged skeleton. Neither changed the files.\n\nEverything is written up in `task_result.md`.",
